# On layouts/push-out-planet.jsonc the stock planet mearth lies at (2500, 2000) and the destroyer Probe 1000 west of it.
# Probe is ordered to the planet's center. It drives in until it meets the planet and the push-out holds it at the
# planet's model radius plus its own model radius from the planet's center, with its order open (move=<x>,<z>), as the
# center lies far outside its tooCloseToTurn.
# Dumps: "before" shows Probe 1000 from the planet's center; "planet" and "planet-later" (10 s on) show it at the same
# distance from the center.
# Run it with --layout layouts/push-out-planet.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
# The point is in the frame of the dump's pos= field, whose z is the layout z mirrored.
wait 1
dump before
box Probe
wait 0.3
move 2500 -2000
wait 40
dump planet
wait 10
dump planet-later
